<tr>
<td background = "images/bar1.gif" height="28"><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#660066" size="3"><font color="#cccccc">Guild Leadership Change and Recruitment Ideas</font></font></td></tr>
<tr><p><td><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#660066" size="2"><font color="#FFFFFF"><br><p>Greetings all!</p><p>
As most of you probably know by now, the guild has undergone a change of leadership. Jedaka has decided to abandon his necro character in favor of his new warrior and because of this, has decided that he is no longer in a position to lead the guild. Jed will still be a member and officer of the guild with his new char so he&#8217;ll still be around on guild chat etc.</p><p>
So as of 2 days ago, I have taken over the leadership of the guild. It&#8217;s a shame to see Jed step down after all his hard work getting the guild up and running but I hope he&#8217;ll still be taking a major role in any decisions affecting the future of the guild.</p><p>
The first thing I want to do is increase our membership. Once we have done this it will be much easier to organise guild events and raids. The first thing I want to do about this is open up membership to people level 20-30 as well as 30+. I have talked to Jed and several other members who have agreed with this plan. I hope nobody I havent spoken to disagrees, but its really difficult to see most of you online and the forums don&#8217;t seem to get read very often. We have several people in that level range who want to join and I don&#8217;t want to keep them waiting too long or they&#8217;ll go elsewhere.</p><p>
The main reason for this is the difficulty in finding anybody over level 30 who isnt already in a guild but actually wants to be in one. Theres also the fact that most people who havent joined a guild by that point all tend to be classes who can solo and therefore can manage quite well without a guild. That&#8217;s why about half of us are necros. So hopefully inviting levels 20-30 will also mean we get more varied classes. Of course we&#8217;ll still be actively  trying to recruit higher level people. And hopefully higher level members can spare some time to help the new recruits get through 20-30 at a decent speed. </p><p>
Can I also ask everyone to keep their eyes open for potential members. If there is anyone who isnt already an officer who feels they would make a good recruiter, let me know.</p><p><b>
Potential Alliance</b></p><p>
Another plan I have in mind is to form an alliance with another guild.  Both myself and Ickybod are good friends with the leader of Cladagh, so my idea is to approach him and see if we can organise regular joint events and raids with them. Their members are on average a little lower than us at the moment but they do have quite a few 30+ members. </p><p>
We should consider alliances with other guilds too. Its all good planning for when the time comes to start raiding the planes/dragons :).</p><p><b>
Training Guild</b></p><p>
A final idea, slightly more unusual than the first two and im not even sure about this myself so I thought I&#8217;d see what everyone thinks, is an idea that my old guild on Brell tried. This is to have a &#8216;training guild&#8217;. Basically the idea is you have a separate section of the guild, with its own leader, events, meetings etc for low level people. The reason for doing this is you get to &#8216;grow your own&#8217; higher levels. You grab them when they&#8217;re young and impressionable, help them out with xp and items and when they are high enough to join the main guild, you already know them and have their loyalty.</p><p>
Just an idea :).</p><p>
</font><p></p></font></td></tr>
<tr><p><td><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#660066" size="2"><font color="#FFFFFF"><i>Submitted By: <a href="mailto:louise.hand@virgin.net">Carramaena</a> on Monday, May 22, 2000</i><p></p></font></font></td></tr>
<tr><td>

<tr>
<td background = "images/bar1.gif" height="28"><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#660066" size="3"><font color="#cccccc">Member Info Pages etc</font></font></td></tr>
<tr><p><td><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#660066" size="2"><font color="#FFFFFF"><br><p>I'm thinking of putting up a little page on the site for each member. So if anybody wants to send me a biography for their character and a screenshot of themselves then I can create a page for you which will be linked to your name on the Roster page. My e-mail address is <a href="mailto:louise.hand@virgin.net">louise.hand@virgin.net</a></p><p>Also, Angarth is thinking of writing something to allow you all to upload your best eq screenshots to the site so we can start a Picture Gallery. So start looking out your best shots :)</p><p>I'll be trying to get some good guild screenshots at the meeting on Saturday, so can everyone polish their armor and get their robes cleaned beforehand :)</p><p>See you all on Saturday</p></font><p></p></font></td></tr>
<tr><p><td><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#660066" size="2"><font color="#FFFFFF"><i>Submitted By: <a href="mailto:louise.hand@virgin.net">Carramaena</a> on Thursday, May 18, 2000</i><p></p></font></font></td></tr>
<tr><td>

<tr>
<td background = "images/bar1.gif" height="28"><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#660066" size="3"><font color="#cccccc">Guild Meeting Saturday!!!</font></font></td></tr>
<tr><p><td><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#660066" size="2"><font color="#FFFFFF"><br>There is a guild meeting scheduled for Saturday the 20th at noon central time.  Attendance is not required,  but HIGHLY suggested,  at least the first 15 minutes of attendance.  In the first 15 minutes of the meeting I will tell the guild about something important and we will decide on a course of action.  I expect all the members who can be there to be there,  as this may affect you personally and you will want to be there to put your voice into it.

The meeting will be held at the Arena which connects to the Lake Rathe zone.

After the meeting we will have a guild brawl in celebration.  I hope to see everyone there,  not only is the guild invited to come but any friends you guys would like to come and have some fun.  </font><p></p></font></td></tr>
<tr><p><td><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#660066" size="2"><font color="#FFFFFF"><i>Submitted By: <a href="mailto:">Jedaka</a> on Wednesday, May 17, 2000</i><p></p></font></font></td></tr>
